  "query_preview": "..\nNot much has changed. A very dry pattern is anchored across the\nMarianas and looks to continue through the end of next week. The only\nexception is for Guam, during the afternoons of Sunday and Monday.\nWith light and variable winds, island convection is expected for both\nafternoons, though Sunday looks to be the better chance out of both\ndays. The one limiting factor will be the available moisture.\nHowever, after TY In-fa departs the region, it looks like PWats\n(Precipitable Water) will increase, possibly over 2 inches. This\nshould allow the island convection to develop. If it does increase\nsufficiently and winds are light enough, the CNMI could also see \nsome island convection. We should have a better idea tomorrow.",
